We adopt this strict full-sequence criterion because it directly addresses the most relevant leakage question: whether a complete downstream test sequence is already present in the corresponding training data. This avoids conflating true train-test leakage with the inherent redundancy of genomic sequences, where short local motifs and partial overlaps are common even among biologically distinct regions.

