3.3. OCR-Style Prompted Pretraining Tasks
To pretrain OpticalDNA, we formulate genomic understanding as an OCR-style prompted learning paradigm over a unified conversation interface. We construct six prompt families (T1-T6) spanning four genomic primitives: recognition, grounding, retrieval, and completion (Table 1; see Appendix C for our design principles). Specifically, T1 performs free-form DNA transcription; T2 couples transcription with spatial grounding; T3 transcribes DNA within given ROIs; T4 completes masked regions within given ROIs; T5 localizes all occurrences of a query subsequence; and T6 predicts a chromosome-level class label.
